.TH NANOSLEEP 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
nanosleep \- suspend execution for a relative interval
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <time.h>
.B int nanosleep(const struct timespec* requested, struct timespec* remaining);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Suspends execution for the relative interval in requested. The Linux timespec
contains long tv_sec and tv_nsec fields. If interrupted, a non\-NULL
remaining receives the unslept interval.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero, or \-1 with errno set, including EINTR on interruption.
Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sleep (3crunch),
.BR nanosleep (2)
